[b]Disclaimer: this mod was made with AI assistance.[/b] If you're not comfortable with that, please stop reading here.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Pasttimes/images/banner.jpg?v=2[/img]

[b]Games to pass the time between runs, for Build 42 multiplayer.[/b] Vanilla already scatters dice, decks of cards, poker chips, checker boards and chess sets around Knox County. Now you can use them.

[table]
[tr][td][b]Game version[/b][/td][td]Build 42 only (42.0+)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Multiplayer[/b][/td][td]Made for it: the server rolls, shuffles, deals and checks every move[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Add mid-save[/b][/td][td]Yes[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Requires[/b][/td][td]Dazed Core[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Mod ID[/b][/td][td]DazedPastimes[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Pasttimes/images/h-dice.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Pasttimes/images/dice.png?v=2[/img]
[b]Dice[/b] – right-click any die (d4 to d20, percentile, bone and wooden dice) to roll it, or roll a handful at once. Everyone nearby sees the result above your head.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Pasttimes/images/h-poker.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Pasttimes/images/poker.png?v=2[/img]
[b]Poker[/b] – Texas hold'em for up to six at any table. Start a game with a deck of cards, buy in with poker chips, and cash out whole chips when you leave. Blinds, all-ins and side pots all work, and nobody can see your cards.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Pasttimes/images/h-board.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Pasttimes/images/board.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Checkers[/b] – English draughts: taking is compulsory, multi-jumps, kings.
[*][b]Chess[/b] – every rule, from castling and en passant to promotion, stalemate and threefold repetition.
[/list]
Right-click a table and pick [i]Table games[/i] to start. Playing eases boredom and unhappiness a little, more so with company (a sandbox switch).

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Pasttimes/images/h-stakes.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Pasttimes/images/stakes.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*][b]High roll[/b] and [b]Liar's dice[/b] – dice games for two to six at a table. The server throws every die, and in liar's dice nobody sees your cup.
[*][b]Stakes[/b] – in checkers, chess and the dice games, put up chips, items or information: a secret note, marks for the winner's map, or a patch of your map to uncover for them. The table holds the stakes and pays the winner. Promises go in writing too, but nobody can make you keep them. Onlookers can back a side with chips.
[/list]

[h2]Sandbox options[/h2]
[list]
[*]Games ease boredom (on)
[*]How far away a dice roll can be seen (10 tiles)
[*]Table chips per Poker Chips item (100)
[*]Poker big blind (10) and turn time (45 s)
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]Build 42 only.
[*]Uses the vanilla items unchanged, so it should sit happily beside most mods. Game Night changes the same items; running both has not been tested.
[/list]

